 immediately upstream S06 ROADM because the available observations provide no positive localization to an earlier node.", "grounded": ["oms.S08-S23|36", "oms.S23-S06|36", "oms.S06-S21|36"], "n_grounded": 3, "note": ""}, {"fault_mode": "AMP_GAIN_TILT", "location_kind": "term", "term": "upstream_amplifier", "anchor_symptom": "O4", "anchor_service": null, "element": null, "probability": 0.06, "rationale": "Gain tilt could selectively weaken och8 while leaving total amplifier input and output power nearly unchanged. It is less favored because the observed channel loss is very large and no amplifier telemetry or pump-current change supports an amplifier fault.", "grounded": [], "n_grounded": 0, "note": "nothing at that location documents the mode"}, {"fault_mode": "SPAN_LOSS_INCREASE", "location_kind": "term", "term": "upstream_span", "anchor_symptom": "O4", "anchor_service": null, "element": null, "probability": 0.01, "rationale": "Added loss on the final span could lower received power and OSNR. It should affect all channels and ordinarily alter downstream amplifier input telemetry or the OSC, neither of which was observed, so it is unlikely.", "grounded": [], "n_grounded": 0, "note": "nothing at that location documents the mode"}, {"fault_mode": "RX_DEGRADATION", "location_kind": "term", "term": "this_unit", "anchor_symptom": "O1", "anchor_service": null, "element": null, "probability": 0.01, "rationale": "Receiver-local degradation could explain the OSNR and BER changes at trx.och8.z. It cannot explain the independent 9.6-level channel-power reduction measured by the S21 OCM, making it only a remote alternative.", "grounded": ["trx.och8.z"], "n_grounded": 1, "note": ""}], "probability_other": 0.03, "sum_stated": 0.96}, "llm": {"provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5.6"}, "llm_calls": [{"role": "proposer", "latency_s": 22.152599096298218, "input_tokens": 9194, "output_tokens": 2150, "reasoning_tokens": 1552, "ok": true, "error": ""}]}